---
/**
 * src/pages/index.astro
 * Main portfolio page per spec Parts B, C, D, E, J.
 */
import Seo from '../components/Seo.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import CaseStudy from '../components/CaseStudy.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import { frozenEngineeringStudies } from '../data/frozen.js';
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
  <Seo />
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#work">Skip to case studies</a>

  <!-- 1. Danfo stripe and Hero -->
  <Hero />

  <!-- 2. Navigation -->
  <Nav />

  <main id="main">
    <!-- 3. Three things I built (FROZEN case studies) -->
    <Section
      id="work"
      headingId="work-h"
      title="Three things I built"
      lede="Each one has a written account of what broke along the way. I specify the design, direct an AI coding agent, then read, test and break what it produces."
    >
      {frozenEngineeringStudies.map(study => (
        <CaseStudy
          title={study.title}
          stack={study.stack}
          problem={study.problem}
          role={study.role}
          whatBuilt={study.whatBuilt}
          keyDecisions={study.keyDecisions}
          result={study.result}
          links={study.links}
        />
      ))}
    </Section>

    <!-- 4. In progress: Rowta, and Also built -->
    <Section
      id="rowta"
      headingId="rowta-h"
      title="In progress: Rowta"
      lede="Shift scheduling for small teams. honest status and architecture."
    >
      <article class="case" aria-labelledby="rowta-title">
        <div>
          <span class="status-chip">In progress. Not launched.</span>
          <p style="margin: 0 0 16px;">Done so far: sign-up and sign-in, sessions, password reset and one-time sign-in links, with a 124-test server suite.</p>
          <h3 id="rowta-title">Rowta, shift scheduling for small teams</h3>
          <p class="stack">Expo (React Native), Android first, Node, TypeScript, Hono, PostgreSQL, Redis, BullMQ, Prisma</p>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>My role</dt>
            <dd>Solo. I wrote the product spec, the design system and the rules for the AI coding agent, directed it phase by phase, and review and test what it produces. I make every git commit myself.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>What is built and checked so far</dt>
            <dd>
              <ul>
                <li>A static web surface with landing page and draft legal pages. Drafts, not lawyer-reviewed, marked as drafts on the site.</li>
                <li>An auth server: Argon2id password hashing, 15-minute access tokens, refresh tokens that rotate and revoke the whole family on reuse, emailed one-time codes (5 minutes, 5 attempts), reset and magic-link sign-in that works once and expires in 5 minutes.</li>
              </ul>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Key decisions</dt>
            <dd>
              <ul>
                <li>Unknown-email and wrong-password paths do the same amount of work, so response time does not reveal which emails have accounts. Found and fixed a real leak. First version: sign-in 1.04, verify-code 1.27, reset-code 1.36 (the last two failed). After removing the difference in database work: 1.00, 1.17, 1.17. After the final change: 1.02, 1.02, 1.08.</li>
                <li>Sign-in link token travels in the URL fragment and is consumed only by a POST, so mail scanners that open links cannot use it up.</li>
                <li>Refresh tokens rotate on every use, and reuse of an old one revokes the whole token family, so a stolen token stops working as soon as the real user refreshes.</li>
              </ul>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Result so far</dt>
            <dd>
              <table class="results-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Measurement</th>
                    <th scope="col">Value</th>
                    <th scope="col">Evidence</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Server test suite</td>
                    <td>17 files / 124 tests / 124 passed</td>
                    <td>Source: Rowta repository (not published yet), docs/gates/phase-2.md</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Timing: unknown account vs wrong password or code (ratio of response times, 1.00 means equal)</td>
                    <td>
                      sign-in 1.02 (38.1 ms vs 38.8 ms), verify-code 1.02 (49.3 ms vs 48.5 ms), reset-code 1.08 (48.3 ms vs 52.2 ms).
                      <div style="margin-top: 4px; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--muted);">55 requests per side after discarding 5, alternating, one development machine. Pass band: at most 1.25.</div>
                    </td>
                    <td>Source: Rowta repository (not published yet), docs/gates/phase-2.md</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Not built yet</dt>
            <dd>
              <ul class="not-built">
                <li>Teams and roles</li>
                <li>Shifts and swaps</li>
                <li>Billing</li>
                <li>Push notifications</li>
                <li>Offline mode</li>
                <li>Load test not run yet</li>
                <li>Deployed backend</li>
                <li>Development build</li>
                <li>Demo video</li>
              </ul>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Next</dt>
            <dd>No dates set yet.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Links</dt>
            <dd>Repo link coming</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </article>

      <!-- Also built: APE-P-I and Daily Meal (spec C8) -->
      <div class="also-built-block" aria-labelledby="also-built-h">
        <h3 id="also-built-h">Also built: a food-delivery API, and an app that proves it works from outside</h3>
        <p class="lede">Two separate projects communicating across domain boundaries with live public endpoints.</p>

        <div class="also-built-grid">
          <article class="case" aria-labelledby="api-h">
            <div>
              <h4 id="api-h">APE-P-I (REST API)</h4>
              <p class="stack">Next.js 15, Prisma 6, PostgreSQL 16</p>
            </div>
            <p>A REST API serving realistic food-delivery data (restaurants, menu items, orders, customers). Seeded with about 40 restaurants, 300 customers and 500 orders. Endpoints: list restaurants (paginated, filterable, sortable), get a restaurant, get its menu, create, get, update status and delete an order. No auth, no admin panel: the endpoints are the product.</p>
            <div class="links">
              <a href="https://github.com/Antisocialworld/APE-P-I">API Code</a>
              <a href="https://ape-p-i.vercel.app">API Live</a>
              <a href="https://github.com/Antisocialworld/APE-P-I/blob/main/DOCUMENTATION.md">API Documentation</a>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="case" aria-labelledby="app-h">
            <div>
              <h4 id="app-h">Daily Meal (API Client App)</h4>
              <p class="stack">Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19), no database</p>
            </div>
            <p>A pure API client. Lists restaurants from the live API, filters by cuisine, paginates with previous/next (offset and limit), handles loading, empty and error states, and calls the API across a real domain boundary (a separate project making real cross-origin requests).</p>
            <div class="links">
              <a href="https://github.com/Antisocialworld/Daily-Meal">App Code</a>
              <a href="https://daily-meal-one.vercel.app">App Live</a>
              <a href="https://github.com/Antisocialworld/Daily-Meal/blob/main/DOCUMENTATION.md">App Documentation</a>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <figure style="margin-top: 24px;">
          <div class="snap-wrap">
            <div class="snap-row snap-col-2" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Daily Meal screens">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img
                  src="/img/d01-daily-meal-list.webp"
                  width="600"
                  height="1135"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  alt="Daily Meal app running on a mobile screen, showing cuisine filter chips and restaurant listing with sample data"
                />
              </div>
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img
                  src="/img/d02-daily-meal-pagination.webp"
                  width="600"
                  height="1186"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  alt="Daily Meal app running on a mobile screen, showing pagination controls with previous and next buttons"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="snap-hint" aria-hidden="true">Swipe to see more screens &rarr;</p>
          </div>
          <figcaption>Daily Meal on a phone: the filter, the list and the previous/next pages. Logo and interface designed by me. The restaurants are sample data from my API.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <!-- 5. What makes me different (spec J8) -->
    <Section
      id="different"
      headingId="different-h"
      title="What makes me different"
      lede="Principles demonstrated by working code and evidence on this page."
    >
      <ul class="different-list">
        <li class="different-item">
          <span class="different-lead">I prove behaviour, not just features.</span>
          <p>Each case study lists the tests I broke it with and what they showed.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="different-item">
          <span class="different-lead">I write down what went wrong.</span>
          <p>Every project has a write-up with the bugs I found and what is not built.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="different-item">
          <span class="different-lead">I design and build.</span>
          <p>Wordmarks, a tech pack, app screens, and a logo taken from a paper sketch to SVG. <a href="#more-design-work">More design work, including recreations I label as recreations.</a></p>
        </li>
        <li class="different-item">
          <span class="different-lead">I direct AI agents and check their work.</span>
          <p>I write the spec, the agent builds, I read, test and break the result, and I make every commit myself.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="different-item">
          <span class="different-lead">Made in Lagos.</span>
          <p>Okada and danfo lettering, naira pricing in the payments work, and a merged pull request adding a Nigeria list to an open source tool.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Section>

    <!-- 6. Design (spec C5, J17, D1, D3, C6) -->
    <Section
      id="design"
      headingId="design-h"
      title="Design"
      lede="From paper sketches to vectors, app design systems, and illustration."
    >
      <!-- Rowta Logo Process (C5) -->
      <article style="margin-bottom: 48px;" aria-labelledby="rowta-logo-h">
        <h3 id="rowta-logo-h">The Rowta logo: from paper to SVG</h3>
        <p>The concept was drawn by hand on paper by me. The final SVG files were generated from my sketches with AI assistance, following my direction, and refined over many rounds of my feedback. I approved every proportion, colour and size rule.</p>
        <p>Locked rules: lettered book at 160 px and up; letterless at 48 px and below (favicon, notification icon); a white silhouette for the notification icon. Colours: tile #292da3, spine #1e227b, pages #d6d7f5, ribbon and tint #7f82dc.</p>

        <div style="margin-top: 16px; max-width: 480px;">
          <Figure
            src="/img/rowta-logo.webp"
            alt="Rowta logo: the word ROWTA in rounded letter tiles on a white book cover with a bookmark, on a blue background."
            width={1024}
            height={538}
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Lettering Process: From pen sketch to final wordmark (spec J17) -->
      <article style="margin-bottom: 48px;" aria-labelledby="lettering-h">
        <h3 id="lettering-h">From pen sketch to final wordmark</h3>
        <p>Pen sketch by me, then redrawn as vector and illustrated in Figma.</p>

        <div class="sketch-grid">
          <!-- Okada reveal card -->
          <figure class="reveal-card" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Okada: sketch and final wordmark comparison">
            <div class="reveal-stage">
              <div class="reveal-base">
                <div class="frame" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4px; width: 100%; background: var(--paper);">
                  <img src="/img/s02-sketch-okada-early.webp" width="386" height="284" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Pen sketch on grid paper showing early motorcycle lettering concept" />
                  <img src="/img/s01-sketch-okada-bike.webp" width="463" height="348" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Pen sketch on grid paper of Okada bike lettering with front wheel" />
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="reveal-overlay">
                <div class="frame" style="width: 100%;">
                  <img src="/img/okada-colour.webp" width="681" height="438" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Final Okada wordmark as a motorcycle with the letter O as front wheel" />
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="reveal-hint" aria-hidden="true">Tap or hover to compare sketch and final wordmark &rarr;</p>
            <figcaption>Okada: pen sketch on squared paper (s01/s02), redrawn as vector with the letter O as the front wheel.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <!-- Danfo reveal card -->
          <figure class="reveal-card" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Danfo: sketch and final artwork comparison">
            <div class="reveal-stage">
              <div class="reveal-base">
                <div class="frame" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4px; width: 100%; background: var(--paper);">
                  <img src="/img/s03-sketch-danfo-wordmark.webp" width="451" height="193" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Pen sketch on grid paper of Danfo bus lettering" />
                  <img src="/img/s04-sketch-danfo-bus.webp" width="451" height="218" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Pen sketch on grid paper of Danfo bus outline" />
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="reveal-overlay">
                <div class="frame" style="width: 100%;">
                  <img src="/img/danfo.webp" width="630" height="585" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Final Danfo bus wordmark in yellow and black linework" />
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="reveal-hint" aria-hidden="true">Tap or hover to compare sketch and final wordmark &rarr;</p>
            <figcaption>Danfo: pen sketch on squared paper (s03/s04), redrawn in yellow and black line work.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <!-- No Evil reveal card -->
          <figure class="reveal-card" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="No Evil: sketch and final illustration comparison">
            <div class="reveal-stage">
              <div class="reveal-base">
                <div class="frame" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4px; width: 100%; background: var(--paper);">
                  <img src="/img/s05-sketch-noevil-faces.webp" width="811" height="309" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Pen sketch of three faces covering eyes, ears, and mouth" />
                  <img src="/img/s06-sketch-noevil-word.webp" width="644" height="348" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Pen sketch of No Evil script lettering" />
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="reveal-overlay">
                <div class="frame" style="width: 100%;">
                  <img src="/img/no-evil.webp" width="1400" height="1081" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Final No Evil illustration of three teal faces labelled See, Hear, and Speak" />
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="reveal-hint" aria-hidden="true">Tap or hover to compare sketch and final wordmark &rarr;</p>
            <figcaption>No Evil: pen sketch of faces and script lettering (s05/s06), redrawn as three teal faces.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Sprint Screens (spec D1) -->
      <article style="margin-bottom: 48px;" aria-labelledby="sprint-h">
        <h3 id="sprint-h">Sprint, a running and fitness app</h3>
        <p>Onboarding and home screens for Sprint, a running and fitness app. Designed by me in Figma.</p>
        <div class="snap-wrap">
          <div class="snap-row sprint-grid" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Sprint screens">
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c03-sprint-flat-home.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Flat UI screen of Sprint fitness app home dashboard showing activity rings and workout statistics" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Onboarding and home screens for Sprint, a running and fitness app. Designed by me in Figma.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c01-sprint-phone-mock-start.webp" width="600" height="338" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Sprint onboarding screen in a handheld phone mockup template" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>The device mockup and the photos in these screens are not mine. The screen designs are.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c02-sprint-phone-mock-home.webp" width="600" height="338" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Sprint home screen shown in a handheld phone mockup template" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>The device mockup and the photos in these screens are not mine. The screen designs are.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <p class="snap-hint" aria-hidden="true">Swipe to see more screens &rarr;</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Perfume Gallery States Grid (spec D3, D4) -->
      <article style="margin-bottom: 48px;" aria-labelledby="perfume-h">
        <h3 id="perfume-h">Perfume Gallery: authentication & state flows</h3>
        <p>Sign-in and registration states for a perfume shop app: empty, error, password strength, account exists, passwords do not match.</p>
        <div class="snap-wrap">
          <div class="snap-row perfume-grid" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Perfume Gallery authentication and state screens">
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c08-perfume-login-empty.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app login screen in empty state with email and password inputs" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Login: empty state.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c04-perfume-login-error.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app login screen displaying inline validation error: incorrect password" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Login: error state.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c05-perfume-register-empty.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app register screen in empty initial state" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Register: empty state.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <div class="strength-strip">
                  <img src="/img/c06-perfume-register-weak.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Password strength weak indicator with red progress bar" />
                  <img src="/img/c11-perfume-register-fair.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Password strength fair indicator with amber progress bar" />
                  <img src="/img/c12-perfume-register-strong.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Password strength strong indicator with green progress bar" />
                </div>
              </div>
              <figcaption>Password meter: weak, fair, and strong indicators.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c10-perfume-account-exists.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app registration displaying alert that account already exists with that email" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Register: account exists alert.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c13-perfume-password-mismatch.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app registration showing error when confirmed password does not match" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Register: password mismatch.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c07-perfume-reset.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app password reset flow screen" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Password reset screen.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="snap-card">
              <div class="frame phone-screen">
                <img src="/img/c18-perfume-drawer.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app navigation drawer open over content" />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Navigation drawer open.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <p class="snap-hint" aria-hidden="true">Swipe to see more screens &rarr;</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Drawing and clothing design gallery (spec C6) -->
      <article aria-labelledby="drawing-gallery-h">
        <h3 id="drawing-gallery-h">Drawing and clothing design</h3>
        <p class="lede">I draw too. All of this is my own work, and the spiral signature is mine.</p>

        <div class="gallery">
          <figure class="g-okada">
            <div class="pair">
              <div class="frame"><img src="/img/okada-colour.webp" width="681" height="438" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The word Okada drawn as a motorbike, in colour. The O is the front wheel." /></div>
              <div class="frame"><img src="/img/okada-line.webp" width="681" height="438" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The same Okada wordmark as plain line work." /></div>
            </div>
            <figcaption>Okada wordmark. The wheel is the O. Shown in colour and as line work.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="g-noevil">
            <div class="frame"><img src="/img/no-evil.webp" width="1400" height="1081" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Three teal faces labelled See, Hear and Speak above the handwritten words No Evil." /></div>
            <figcaption>See, hear, speak no evil, redrawn as three faces.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="g-tee">
            <div class="frame tint"><img src="/img/spooky-man-techpack.webp" width="567" height="800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A tech pack for a black tee called Spooky Man, with front and back views and print details in green." /></div>
            <figcaption>Spooky Man tee. Tech pack with front and back views and the print details.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="g-woman">
            <div class="frame"><img src="/img/portrait-woman.webp" width="900" height="1144" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Vector illustration of a woman with a high curly bun, pink diamond earrings and a purple wrap top." /></div>
            <figcaption>Character illustration.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="g-man">
            <div class="frame"><img src="/img/portrait-man.webp" width="1100" height="1043" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Vector illustration of a bearded man in a teal and black short-sleeve shirt on a yellow background." /></div>
            <figcaption>Character illustration.</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <figure class="g-habitat">
            <div class="frame"><img src="/img/c14-music-is-my-habitat-illustration.webp" width="1000" height="1701" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Music is my habitat illustration featuring yellow character, boombox, and headphones" /></div>
            <figcaption>Music is my habitat illustration.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- More design work (spec ASSETS-PASS2.md) -->
      <details id="more-design-work" class="more-design-details">
        <summary class="more-design-summary">More design work</summary>
        <div class="more-design-content">
          <!-- 1. Logo (first) -->
          <article aria-labelledby="sportsvill-h">
            <h4 id="sportsvill-h" style="font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 12px;">Logo design</h4>
            <figure>
              <div class="frame" style="max-width: 320px;">
                <img
                  src="/img/l01-sportsvill24-logo.webp"
                  width="600"
                  height="597"
                  loading="lazy"
                  decoding="async"
                  alt="Round green logo: a stick figure kicking a ball above the text SV24 and Sportsvill24"
                />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Logo for Sportsvill24, a WhatsApp football group. Designed by me.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </article>

          <!-- 2. Perfume Gallery product screens -->
          <article aria-labelledby="perfume-products-h">
            <h4 id="perfume-products-h" style="font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 12px;">Perfume Gallery product screens</h4>
            <figure>
              <div class="snap-wrap">
                <div class="snap-row snap-col-4" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Perfume Gallery product screens">
                  <div class="frame phone-screen">
                    <img src="/img/p01-perfume-luxury-oil.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app luxury oil product view with price and add to cart" />
                  </div>
                  <div class="frame phone-screen">
                    <img src="/img/p02-perfume-list.webp" width="600" height="1298" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Perfume app catalog list layout showing fragrance cards" />
